  "notes": "{積|つ}もる is an intransitive godan verb meaning to pile up or accumulate.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- {自動詞|じどうし}: {積|つ}もる (to pile up)\n- {他動詞|たどうし}: {積|つ}む (to pile, load)\n\nSENSE 1 (physical accumulation):\n- {雪|ゆき}が{積|つ}もる: snow piles up\n- {埃|ほこり}が{積|つ}もる: dust accumulates\n- {落|お}ち{葉|ば}が{積|つ}もる: fallen leaves pile up\n\nSENSE 2 (abstract accumulation):\n- {不満|ふまん}が{積|つ}もる: frustration builds up\n- {疲|つか}れが{積|つ}もる: fatigue accumulates\n- ストレスが{積|つ}もる: stress builds up\n\nIDIOMS:\n- {積|つ}もる{話|はなし}: much to talk about ({話|はなし}が{積|つ}もっている)\n- {塵|ちり}も{積|つ}もれば{山|やま}となる: many a little makes a mickle (proverb)\n\nRELATED:\n- {積|つ}み{重|かさ}ねる: to accumulate (efforts, experience)\n- {蓄積|ちくせき}: accumulation (noun)",
